Short version: the data isn’t actually being lost in the file. Excel always stores the full-precision number (0.123456) — the “0.12” is just a display mask applied by the cell’s number format. So nothing is truncated at the source. Your preprocessor is reading the formatted/displayed text of each cell instead of the stored value. Read the real value and the digits come back.

The fix depends on how the package reads the workbook. The usual culprits:

If it’s a Script Task using Excel Interop, the tell-tale is .Text. .Text returns the formatted string (“0.12”); .Value2 returns the raw underlying double. Switch to .Value2:

// Bad — returns the displayed/formatted string
object cellVal = range.Text;        // "0.12"

// Good — returns full-precision value
object cellVal = range.Value2;      // 0.123456


(.Value also preserves precision, but .Value2 is the safest since it won’t reinterpret currency/dates.)

If it’s OpenXML SDK, the full value lives in the cell’s <v> element. The truncation happens when code applies the cell’s number-format string to produce a display value. For the CSV, just emit the raw value and skip the format:

string raw = cell.CellValue?.InnerText;  // "0.123456" — write this


If it’s EPPlus / ClosedXML, use cell.Value (the object/double), never cell.Text (formatted).

If it’s actually a Data Flow with an Excel Source (ACE/Jet OLE DB), the driver already returns the full numeric value, so this symptom usually wouldn’t appear there — which is another reason I suspect a custom text-reading step.

One gotcha after you fix the read: make sure the CSV writer doesn’t re-round or flip to scientific notation. Format with invariant culture and a round-trip specifier, e.g. ((double)val).ToString("R", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture).

To confirm the values are genuinely intact before you change anything, just widen the column or bump the decimal places in Excel — you’ll see the full 0.123456 sitting there.

How is the conversion actually done — a Script Task (and if so, Interop, OpenXML, or EPPlus?) or a Data Flow with an Excel Source? Tell me which and I’ll give you the exact code change.